","To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, follow these steps:

1. **Understand the concentration:** The concentration is 0.044% (w/v), which means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride are present in 100 mL of Phos-Flur Rinse.

2. **Convert the concentration to grams per mL:**
   \[
   \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.0044 \text{ g/mL}
   \]

3. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**
   \[
   0.044 \text{ g/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.44 \text{ g}
   \]

4. **Convert grams to milligrams:**
   \[
   0.44 \text{ g} \times 100 \text{ mg/g} = 44 \text{ mg}
   \]

