\]
We use the heat change equation:
\[
\DeltaH = \DeltaH_{\text{product}} - \DeltaH_{\text{reactants}}
\]
The reaction can be broken down into the following steps:
1. Formation of the complex \( \text{Fe}(2+} \text{H}_2\text{O}\text{6}^2] \).
2. Formation of the complex \( \text{Fe}(4\text{Cl}\text{2}^{-}\) .
3. Hydrolysis of \( \text{Cl}^- \) to form \( \text{H}_2\text{O} \).

