5. The peak current of the cyclic voltogram is proportional to the concentration of the analyte and the current density. The peak current can be used to determine the concentration of the analyte in the sample.

In summary, cyclic voltamography can detect EC reactions by monitoring the current generated during the electrochemical process. The shape of the cyclic voltogram provides information about the mechanism of the electrochemical reaction, and the peak current can be used to determine the concentration of the analyte in the solution.
