","The reaction is the formation of ethyl alcohol and water from acetic acid and ethyl alcohol, which is an esterification reaction:
\[ \text{CH}_3\text{COOH} + \text{C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH} \rightarrow \text{CH}_3\text{C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \]
The initial concentrations are:
\[ \text{[ CH}_3\text{COOH} \right] = 1 \quad \text{mol} \]
\[ \text{[ C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH } \right) = 1 \quad \text{mol} \]
At equilibrium, the number of moles of unreacted acetic acid is 0.333 mol. This means that the number of moles of acetic acid consumed is:
\[ 1 - 0.333 = 0.677 \, \text{mol} \]
Since the reaction is 1:1, the number of moles of ethanol consumed is also 0.677 mol.
At equilibrium, the number of moles of each product is equal to the number of moles consumed:
\[ \text{[ CH}_3\text{C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH } \right) = 0.677 \, \text{ mol} \]
\[ \text{[ H}_2\text{O } \right) = 0.677 \, \text{ mol} \]
At equilibrium, the concentrations are:
\[ \text{[ CH}_3\text{COOH } \right) = 0.333 \, \text{ mol} \]
\[ \text{[ C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH } \right) = 1 - 0.677 = 0.323 \, \text{ mol} \]
\[ \text{[ CH}_3\text{C}_2H}_5\text{OH } \right) = 0.677 \, \text{ mol} \]
\[ \text{[ H}_2\text{O } \right) = 0.677 \, \text{ mol} \]
The equilibrium constant (K) is given by:
\[ K = \frac{[\text{CH}_3\text{C}_2H}_5\text{OH}] [\text{H}_2\text{O}]]}{ [\text{CH}_3\text{COOH}] [\text{C}_2\text{H}_5\text{OH}} \]
