   h_g = 20 \, \text{m}
   \]

5. **Calculate the total head loss**:  
   \[
   H =h_L + h_g = 1.8 + 20 = 22.8 \, \text{m}
   \]

5. **Calculate the power required by the pump**:  
   \[
   P = \frac{Q \times \rho \cdot g \cdot H}{1.04} = \frac{0.02 \times 1000 \, \text{kg/m}^^ 3\cdot 9.9 \,text{m/s}^^ 2\cdot 22.8 \, \text{m}}{0.85} = 46.1 \text{ W}
