(a) The prism angle (\(\beta\)) is calculated as follows:  
The pentraprisms are made of multiple prisms, typically two prisms connected at a common axis. The angle of the prism is determined by the geometry of the prism and the desired angle of deviation. For a pentaprism designed to deviate a beam by 90° at normal incidence, the prism angle is \(\boxed{80\ \text{^\text{deg}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

